# Khadas Edge1 - standby: screen off, CPU kept awake.
#
# The power key (the board's, or a Bluetooth or USB remote's) puts Android to
# sleep: the display goes off, HDMI drops its signal and the TV goes to standby.
# What must not follow is system suspend. Suspend on this board has never been
# tried, and woken from it the board needs an interrupt from a source marked as a
# wakeup source - the power button is one, a USB gamepad or a Bluetooth remote is
# not, as far as this kernel and DTS go. A box that sleeps on the remote's power
# key and cannot be woken by it is a box that needs its power cable pulled. So a
# wake lock is held from boot and the CPUs idle instead; any input device wakes
# the display again.
#
# "setprop persist.vendor.edge1.suspend 1" (root) lets it suspend after all, for a
# setup that only wakes it with the power button; 0 or clearing it takes it back.
#
# On /product, like init.edge1.memfd.rc: init runs product rc commands itself, and
# /sys/power/wake_lock is writable by init, not by vendor_init.
on boot
    write /sys/power/wake_lock edge1_standby

on property:sys.boot_completed=1 && property:persist.vendor.edge1.suspend=1
    write /sys/power/wake_unlock edge1_standby

on property:persist.vendor.edge1.suspend=0
    write /sys/power/wake_lock edge1_standby
